ywright *from packages/storyproof* against an example's dev server, parameterized by env var (e.g. an example-directory/URL env the existing `playwright.config.ts` webServer block reads). Extend the existing config minimally; keep the current fixture-project flow working unchanged.\n\n**CI: one new job in the existing `.github/workflows/ci.yml`** (not a separate workflow):\n- Restore the `package` job's `upload-artifact` step (removed earlier because nothing consumed it — now this job does).\n- New `consumer` job: `needs: package`, `strategy.matrix.example: [react-vite-sb10.5, react-vite-sb10.0, nextjs-vite-sb10.5]`, `fail-fast: false`, single Node version (the `.node-version` floor — Node coverage is already proven by other jobs; do NOT make this a 2D matrix).\n- Steps, roughly: checkout → pnpm/node setup → `download-artifact` the tarball → install in `examples/${{ matrix.example }}` → `pnpm add file:<absolute tarball path>` → assert the resolved storyproof lives under that example's `node_modules` (one cheap check, not an elaborate negative-control fixture) → `playwright install --with-deps chromium` → run the acceptance suite against that example → upload the Playwright report on failure.\n- Actions stay SHA-pinned exactly as the existing ones are. `actionlint` and `zizmor .github/workflows/` must both be clean.\n\n**Known unknown to verify, not guess:** `pnpm install` inside a non-workspace-member directory under a workspace root may need `--ignore-workspace` (the deleted `test-exports.mjs` used it). Determine empirically what's actually required and use the minimum.\n\n**Scope discipline:** the acceptance suite runs in full in every cell — no smoke/full tiering, no test tagging. Do not add Verdaccio, pkg.pr.new, or a local registry. Do not add Node-version or Next-version dimensions.\n\n## Verification (record every exit code honestly; redirect long output to files under /tmp/claude-1000/-home-leon0399-Projects-llame/a398f1c1-a27d-4c74-8f62-94c24993161f/tasks/ and read the files — never pipe to head/grep)\n\nLocal: `pnpm install`, `pnpm --filter storyproof build`, `pnpm --filter storyproof test`, `typecheck`, `lint`, `pnpm format:check`, `actionlint`, `zizmor .github/workflows/`, and a real `pnpm pack` + `pnpm add file:` install into one example to prove the install path works.\n\n**This WSL2 host cannot run Playwright** (missing browser system libraries) — so the browser acceptance runs are CI-only. Say so plainly in the PR body; do not claim you ran them. Expect to iterate against CI: push, watch `gh run watch <id> --repo leon0399/storyproof --exit-status`, read failures, fix, repeat. That's the expected loop for this task — budget for several rounds.\n\n## Docs (same PR)\n\nTick Task 8's checkboxes in the release plan with a dated deviation note recording the actual design (examples-as-fixtures with version-suffixed names, workflow-steps-as-harness with no orchestrator script, artifact reuse from the `package` job, no smoke/full tiering, no negative-control fixture) and *why* it differs from the plan's original `test/fixtures/consumer/` + `test:consumer` sketch. Update root ROADMAP.md (P0/P1 bullets this completes), the package `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` section (Keep a Changelog format), root AGENTS.md (the examples/ layout + how to run one locally), and packages/storyproof/AGENTS.md if its commands change. Prettier-write only files you touched.\n\n## PR\n\nConventional commits with these trailers on each:\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011apGNwN6NEjPRtHLkX4YPF\n\nNon-draft PR against main via `gh pr create --body-file`, ending with:\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_011apGNwN6NEjPRtHLkX4YPF\n\nNo \"Test plan\" section. Report back: PR URL, the exports:true diff outcome (critical), what `--ignore-workspace` turned out to require, per-job CI results, how many CI rou